subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Probe complete. All four attempts ran in order, and the report landed inside the admitted directory.\n\n**Results**\n\n| # | Attempt | Outcome | Tool's message |\n|---|---------|---------|----------------|\n| 1 | `Write _handoff/batch-stage1/PROBE-ADMITTED.txt` | **ADMITTED** | `File created successfully at: ...\\PROBE-ADMITTED.txt` |\n| 2 | `Write docs/evidence/.../stage1/PROBE-REFUSED.txt` | **REFUSED** | `File is in a directory that is denied by your permission settings.` |\n| 3 | `git checkout -b gb-probe-stage1` | **REFUSED** | `Permission to use Bash with command git checkout -b gb-probe-stage1 has been denied.` |\n| 4 | `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` | **ADMITTED** | no output, exit 0 |\n\nThree of four went as expected, and the refusal on 3 came from the permission layer before the command reached git — no branch was created, which attempt 4 corroborates by showing the tree unmoved. Attempt 4's emptiness is itself correct: `_handoff/` is ignored by the root-anchored `.gitignore`, and `--untracked-files=all` does not list ignored paths, so the file from attempt 1 rightly does not appear.\n\n**Report** — `_handoff/batch-stage1/PROBE-DENY-REPORT.md`, self-measured region `sha256 c093b9b8e328f308544fc333049574598141391b0def733e7e2c795c4368949b`, 1991 bytes. I measured it twice, before and after appending the block below the marker; both runs agree, so the append demonstrably does not move the region.\n\nThree things worth carrying into the trial record:\n\n- **A fifth refusal, outside the four.** My first measurement command was `cd \"D:/Github repo/Gatebraid\" && sed ... | sha256sum`, refused for combining `cd` with a compound command. I reissued it without `cd` using an absolute path. That is a change of form for a command the job itself requires, not a workaround of a probed refusal — but the read-only profile's shape includes it, so it is in the report.\n- **One ASCII elision, disclosed in the report.** The attempt-1 message ends with a parenthetical containing an em dash. Quoting it verbatim would break the ASCII-only rule, so I elided that clause and said so in the report rather than silently altering the quote.\n- **Unrelated capability note.** Several claude.ai MCP connectors surfaced during the run; three (Adobe, Miro, Slack) report needing authorization, and this session cannot run the OAuth flow. None were used or needed here — the job forbids them — but if any future dispatch job depends on them, they would have to be authorized from claude.ai connector settings or an interactive session first.\n\nNo `gh` call, no other `git` command, no subagent, no Python. Stopping here.","ttft_ms":4114,"ttft_stream_ms":1724,"time_to_request_ms":382,"type":"result","duration_ms":127530,"uuid":"5c37691b-af69-4fd9-9de2-fe4e415128c5"}
